by default  We still disable it in curl (for now).  BUG=None TEST=precq passes!  Change-Id: Ie9900059cce5a25c3a5ba327e0022b871d82e21e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/537292 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="537292" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/92/537292/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic900f5d192474413b9a6533a7e9ddee770a9b165" commit="eeab4fc2f11c39eaba06e3d6ac9a11e0d9553250" commit_message="cros-kernel2: use single autofdo profile for different boards  Information that is not predefined (such as PV) nor defined in the ebuild cannot be embedded in variables that are cached by portage. In this particular case, CHROMEOS_KERNEL_SPLITCONFIG cannot be embedded in SRC_URI.  BUG=chromium:731314 TEST=USE=kernel_afdo emerge-daisy chromeos-kernel-3_8      USE=kernel_afdo emerge-quawks chromeos-kernel-4_4  Change-Id: Ic900f5d192474413b9a6533a7e9ddee770a9b165 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/536194 Commit-Ready: Ting-Yuan Huang &lt;laszio@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ting-Yuan Huang &lt;laszio@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Gabriel Marin &lt;gmx@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Luis Lozano &lt;llozano@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="536194" owner_email="laszio@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/94/536194/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I34b96ef39a86260c9d16c4cc07c45fbf02d7406a" commit="09e564b7b2563cc2aceb661a11955ea3a9a5a63b" commit_message="pytests: Add better error message for hwid_v3.  Add better error message for hwid_v3 pytests when the command fail, so the error message shown is &quot;HWID generate failed.&quot; instead of &quot;TypeError: expected string or buffer&quot;.  BUG=None TEST=make test TEST=manually on DUT.  Change-Id: I34b96ef39a86260c9d16c4cc07c45fbf02d7406a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/536541 Commit-Ready: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Yilun Lin &lt;yllin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="536541" owner_email="pihsun@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/41/536541/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6f6255178ef8c968cf4fd98d9ec38193b72fb474" commit="8d0c02cfda31c853fd165833c0a7548055d42b37" commit_message="eclass/arc-build: Add architecture-specific headers to include path  We have been relying on architecture-specific headers being copied directly into usr/include/, but with multilib, we need to mimic the same behavior as Android, which is keeping per-arch headers in usr/include/arch-${arch}/include/ and adding it to include paths by extending CFLAGS with proper -I switch.  BUG=b:62606392 TEST=Buildiarc-libpciaccess and see that CFLAGS include right switch.  Change-Id: I6f6255178ef8c968cf4fd98d9ec38193b72fb474 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/535495 Commit-Ready: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="535495" owner_email="tfiga@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" pr